WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.400
- You know I love closing the show

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.860
with something sure to make you smile.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:04.303
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:07.690
(upbeat music)
(crowd cheering)

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.320
Bright yellow refrigerators are popping up

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.550
on sidewalks across Philadelphia.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.900
They're filled with fresh food
and water for anyone to grab.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.990
The motto is take what you
need, leave what you don't.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.980
The goal is to combat food scarcity

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.530
and it's all thanks to the
community fridge project,

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.460
launched by the e-commerce
company, Mama-Tee.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.510
You can read all about it

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:29.200
in "People" magazine's
annual kindness issue,

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.870
on newsstands stands today.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.290
This special issue highlights

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.240
do-gooders all over the country.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.510
We have the woman behind the
community fridge project,

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.440
joining us right now.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.927
Let's say "Hi," to people's
kindness award winner, Michelle.

00:00:40.927 --> 00:00:41.939
(crowd cheering)

00:00:41.939 --> 00:00:45.340
Hi Michelle!

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.140
- Good to be here with you.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.930
- Oh, you have a beautiful smile.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.785
You just made me smile with your smile.

00:00:50.785 --> 00:00:51.840
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.030
Well, how did you come up with this idea?

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:58.450
- Well, I don't think people
know that Philadelphia is one

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:02.790
of the most food insecure
cities across the country.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:06.730
One in five Philadelphians
suffer from some level

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.140
of food insecurity, and I always wanted

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.990
to be involved in a
socially impactful mission.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.150
I'm a past educator.

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:15.580
That was very important for me

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.350
to also provide an example for kids

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:21.240
to be responsible citizens.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:25.290
And so the community fridges
was just a right fit for me.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:28.220
And now we have 18.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.053
- That's amazing.
(crowd applauding)

00:01:29.053 --> 00:01:31.350
And thank you for being
an educator, by the way.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:35.310
You're featured in "People"
magazine's kindness issue.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.710
So what does kindness mean to you?

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:40.790
- Kindness means the world to me.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:43.500
This project has let me know

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.130
that there are some
wonderful humans out there,

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.690
no matter how big or
small we can all help out.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.530
And your help is unique to you.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.930
I just think the main thing
is that we all get involved.

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.170
- Absolutely.
(crowd applauding)

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.240
Well, we want to thank "People" magazine

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.950
for bringing us this incredible story.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:03.770
To read more inspiring stories
from the kindness issue,

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.170
please pick up the new issue of "People"

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.990
on newsstands nationwide, right now,

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:09.080
you're gonna want to check it out.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.210
Thank you so much, Michelle,
for all that you're doing,

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:13.286
I'm liking your posts right now, right?

00:02:13.286 --> 00:02:14.505
(heart dinging)
(crowd cheering)

00:02:14.505 --> 00:02:16.417
(Michelle laughing)
- [Michelle] Thank you, Kelly.

00:02:16.417 --> 00:02:18.840
- And that's not all,
our season long partner,

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.030
Pilot Pen, the go-to pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.550
likes to celebrate those
who create fearlessly,

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:24.590
just like you ma'am.

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:27.180
So they'll be using their G2 gel ink pen

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.020
to write you a check
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:30.043
How's that sound?

00:02:30.043 --> 00:02:32.053
(crowd cheering)

00:02:32.053 --> 00:02:33.326
- Thank you, that's awesome.

00:02:33.326 --> 00:02:34.696
- Yeah!
(both laughing)

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:37.146
All right, thank you
Michelle, have a lovely day.

